6295:The first symbolic attempt exposed a real semantic issue rather than a bad test: pure K functions do not case-split on an unknown Boolean guard during reachability proof. I’m changing the evaluator to an explicit small-step machine, so each Python `if` becomes two constrained transitions at the top of the `<k>` cell. That gives `kprove` the path split it needs and more accurately models evaluation order.
